{"name":"Crash Dummy","hex":"#eeee66","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crash dummy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of crash test dummy.","One who is prone to crashing out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash_dummy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crash test dummy","blocks":[{"text":"A crash test dummy, or simply dummy, is a full-scale anthropomorphic test device (ATD) that simulates the dimensions, weight proportions and articulation of the human body during a traffic collision. Dummies are used by researchers, automobile and aircraft manufacturers to predict the injuries a person might sustain in a crash. Modern dummies are usually instrumented to record data such as velocity of impact, crushing force, bending, folding, or torque of the body, and deceleration rates during a collision."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/CEP1710-58.jpg/330px-CEP1710-58.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crash_test_dummy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/B11510P002.jpg/500px-B11510P002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/B11510P002.jpg/1280px-B11510P002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/B11510P002.jpg/500px-B11510P002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cadaver used during a frontal impact test.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AB11510P002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rocket_sled_track.jpg/500px-Rocket_sled_track.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rocket_sled_track.jpg/12